# Production defaults, committed on purpose.
#
# WHY: the frontend deploys to Vercel, the FastAPI backend does not (it needs a
# filesystem, a database, FAISS and Celery). Without this flag a production build
# renders "Cannot reach the API" on every card, which is a poor showing for an
# application that is otherwise complete. Demo mode answers the same API surface
# from generated data inside the browser, and the UI labels itself accordingly.
#
# WHEN TO CHANGE IT: once the backend is deployed somewhere reachable, set
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=false and NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL to its /api/v1 URL, either
# here or as environment variables in the Vercel project (dashboard values win
# over this file). Both are read at BUILD time, so redeploy after changing them.
#
# SCOPE: this file affects `next build` only. `npm run dev` is untouched.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=true
